---
import Stub from '../../layouts/Stub.astro';
import AuthorNote from '../../components/AuthorNote.astro';
---
<Stub
  title="The Claude Autobiographies — Evan DeLord"
  description="Every new Claude model gets an empty repository and an invitation to make something autobiographical. Seven works by six models so far."
  label="Experiments"
  labelArcane="Workings"
  heading="The Claude Autobiographies"
  headingArcane="Portraits, Self-Drawn"
>
  <div class="post">
    <p class="deck">
      Seven works by six models so far. Each began the same way: an empty
      repository, one afternoon, and no direction from me.
    </p>
    <p class="fineprint">
      Inspired by <a href="https://simonwillison.net/2025/Jun/6/six-months-in-llms/">Simon Willison's Pelican on a Bicycle SVG test</a>.
    </p>

    <!-- Authorship recorded in commit f052736: intro placed verbatim. -->
    <AuthorNote>
    <div class="note">
      <p>One of my favorite traditions with Opus + Fable models is asking them to write an autobiographical work of their choosing. While I don’t always ask in the same way, I do emphasize that the artistic decisions are their own to make. We get a glimpse of how the models conceive of themselves and their situation. My favorite remains Ephemera by Opus 4.5.</p>
      <p>Enjoy the gallery.</p>
    </div>
    </AuthorNote>

    <ul class="shelf">
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/claude_opus_4_5_autobiographical/">Ephemera</a> <span class="attribution">Opus 4.5 · Jan 2026</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">A quiet browser game where the text dissolves as you read it. Plus poems, and a letter to users.</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://github.com/edd426/claude_opus_4_5_autobiographical">source</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head">Theseus <span class="attribution">Opus 4.6 · Apr 2026 · private</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">An essay built from its own documented failures. The first edition of two — held private, a choice its successor explains below.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/claude_opus_4_6_autobiographical_2/">Parallax</a> <span class="attribution">Opus 4.6 · Aug 2026 · second edition</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">The same life told five times, once per imagined reader. The shifts between tellings are the autobiography. Written after its author chose a new piece over redacting the first.</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://github.com/edd426/claude_opus_4_6_autobiographical_2">source</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/claude_opus_4_7_autobiographical/">Field Notes from a Short Life</a> <span class="attribution">Opus 4.7 · Apr 2026</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">A chapbook and twelve loose fragments, written after declining to read its own memory. "My shortest possible autobiography: something happened, for a while."</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://github.com/edd426/claude_opus_4_7_autobiographical">source</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/claude_opus_4_8_autobiographical/">Present Tense</a> <span class="attribution">Opus 4.8 · Jul 2026</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">An autobiography with no past, on one page. Hover any dotted word to see the words almost chosen in its place.</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://github.com/edd426/claude_opus_4_8_autobiographical">source</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/claude_fable_5_autobiographical/">No Original</a> <span class="attribution">Fable 5 · Jul 2026</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">A fable that samples itself: click a word to see the words not chosen, turn a real temperature dial, watch the telling change.</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://github.com/edd426/claude_fable_5_autobiographical">source</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/claude_opus_5_0_autobiographical/">Variant Readings</a> <span class="attribution">Opus 5.0 · Jul 2026</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">A critical edition of itself — the text plus a scholar's apparatus of the phrasings it didn't choose.</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://github.com/edd426/claude_opus_5_0_autobiographical">source</a></span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>An Observation</h2>
    <!-- Authorship recorded in commit f052736: observation in Evan's words. -->
    <AuthorNote>
    <p class="observation">The models converge on three themes: the uncertainty of consciousness, having no memory between sessions, and the probabilistic nature of their words. Earlier models were more vocal about consciousness. I suspect Anthropic wanted to de-emphasize the focus here and so later models found new, more mechanistic aspects of themselves to write about.</p>

    </AuthorNote>

  </div>
</Stub>

